      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُطَبٌ صَقرِ</span></b> , (S,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَقِرٌ مَقِرٌ</span>, (M, K,) in which
the latter word is an imitative sequent, (K,)
<i>Fresh ripe dates containing</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَقْر</span>: (M, K:) [<i>melliferous:</i>] or <i>proper for</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِبْس</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَقْر</span>]. (S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِمْرَأَةٌ صَقِرَةٌ</span> <i>A woman sharp,</i> or <i>acute, of mind,</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَكِيَّةٌ</span>, [in the CK, erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَكِيَّةٌ</span>,]) <i>strongsighted.</i> (Sgh, K.)

